HDR output metadata and cache correctness for wlroots 0.20.2

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

EDID retention and color-management primary/target luminance separation,
reference headroom handling and output-change notifications are adapted from
Aqueous patches 0005 and 0006, Zoey Bauer, GPL-3.0-only:
https://github.com/Seafoam-Labs/Aqueous/tree/e52a8cddc93be2a5259de0240660fbc5d7ed85e4/compositor/patches/wlroots
Scoped to protocol v2; no Windows-BT2100, hardware-color-pipeline or compositor
rewrite. Local additions propagate the preferred target via the same output
helper and key the rendering cache on the encoding that was actually composed.

